{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 107, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding the input-to-output residual where none existed gives much larger gains than swapping out an existing conv or pool on that edge (exp 11 vs 12-14), especially on ImageNet16-120."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Without the edge-3 residual, a skip on edge 5 supplies a missing identity path to the output; with the residual present it is redundant or harmful (exp 82,85,87,89 vs 81,84,86,88)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a conv on a previously removed edge contributes new capacity and a new path, unlike replacing an existing pool or 1x1 op (exp 1-2 vs 3-4, 7)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Placing a pool on an empty node1-to-output edge adds an extra aggregation path, whereas replacing a conv or skip loses capacity (exp 43,47,50 vs 41,42,44,46)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Without the residual edge, adding a conv path from node 1 to the output matters much more for gradient flow and capacity (exp 100 vs 91-96)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When edge 1 is already absent, removing edge 0 disconnects nodes 1 and 2 from the input and collapses the cell (exp 27,28 vs others)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Without the input-to-output skip, cutting edge 0 can leave the output with no path to the input, which is catastrophic (exp 27)."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If node 2 has no outgoing edge, adding a conv into node 2 is a dead end that cannot reach the output (exp 52,54,56,58 vs paired 51,53,55,57)."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 5 removed, computation flowing into node 2 never reaches the output, so upgrading edge 2 is wasted (exp 32,36,38 vs 31,35,37)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "In parameter-free, pool-dominated cells the residual skip lets the identity overwhelm the weak signal and sharply hurts accuracy (exp 15,16)."}], "tok": 31781, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "none", "none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "none", "none", "none", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["none", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "skip_connect", "none", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["none", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "none", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_co